
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Host tests
----------

The files here are host checks built with plain g++, not PlatformIO tests.
Each carries its own build line in its header comment; run from the repo root.

  test_loop_scaling.cpp    4-20 mA scaling arithmetic, include/loop_scaling.h.
  test_can_event_mask.cpp  CAN error-event classification, include/can_event_mask.h.
  test_j1939_replay.cpp    J1939 decode replayed over a candump log,
                           include/j1939_decode.h. Takes the log path as argument.
  test_pn532.cpp           PN532 frames, the tag's wire and screen forms, the scan
                           rules and the step driver, include/pn532.h (FW-1).
  test_hmi_buttons.cpp     Lid button debounce, queue, repeat, KEY STUCK,
                           include/hmi_buttons.h (FW-2).
  test_cmd_id.cpp          Board command ids across simulated reboots,
                           include/cmd_id.h (FW-5).
  test_panel_client.cpp    Panel request bodies, mc rules, JSON scan, and the
                           one-call-per-pass HTTP stages, include/panel_client.h
                           and include/mc_value.h (FW-4, FW-8).
  test_hmi_menu.cpp        The screens and flows, include/hmi_menu.h (FW-3, FW-6,
                           FW-8).

  Each exits with its failure count.
